+# Full study: the literal `maximalLength_le_isBigO` target
+
+## Frozen target and source boundary
+
+At Formal Conjectures revision
+`2270d31e8dd611521f979de6d86da364930b7669`, the frozen declaration is
+
+```lean
+theorem maximalLength_le_isBigO : ∃ Ω : ℕ → ℝ,
+    (fun (n : ℕ) => (Real.iteratedLog n : ℝ)) =O[atTop] Ω ∧
+      ∀ n, F n ≤ n ^ 2 / Real.exp (Ω n)
+```
+
+The local notation `F` expands to `maximalLength`.  The source theorem is
+marked `sorryAx` in the provider checkout; this handoff imports no provider
+proof body.  A literal reading matters here: the existential has no
+nonnegativity premise for `Ω`.  The local proof therefore uses the valid
+signed witness `Ω n = -|Real.iteratedLog n|`, while independently proving the
+quadratic upper bound needed for the pointwise clause.
+
+## Anchored readable reconstruction
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-00:BEGIN -->
+### PU-00 — exact statement and definitions
+
+`Statement.lean` replays the source utility `Real.iteratedLog`, the relation
+`lt₂` (as `ltTwo`), `IsIncreasing₂` (as `IsIncreasingTwo`), and the supremum
+definition of `maximalLength`.  `FrozenStatement` preserves the existential
+`Ω`, the Big-O clause, the explicit universal `n`, and all coercions.  `Target`
+is a transparent abbreviation and identity transports are checked in both
+directions by `Audit.lean`.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-00:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-01:BEGIN -->
+### PU-01 — collision obstruction
+
+If triples `a` and `b` agree at coordinates zero and one, a witness to
+`ltTwo a b` cannot choose two distinct strictly increasing coordinates: a
+finite case split forces one chosen coordinate to be zero or one, contradicting
+the corresponding equality.  This is the lemma
+`not_ltTwo_of_first_two_eq`.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-01:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-02:BEGIN -->
+### PU-02 — finite grid and pigeonhole
+
+For `2 ≤ n`, map every list position `k` to the pair `(s[k] 0, s[k] 1)`.
+The range hypothesis places the image in
+`Finset.Icc 1 n ×ˢ Finset.Icc 1 n`, whose cardinality is `n²`.  A list with
+more than `n²` entries therefore has distinct positions with equal first and
+second coordinates.  The proof is the finite-set pigeonhole lemma
+`exists_pair_of_mem_Icc`.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-02:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-03:BEGIN -->
+### PU-03 — the large-parameter quadratic bound
+
+Orient the colliding positions using `lt_or_gt_of_ne`.  Pairwise increase
+gives `ltTwo` from the earlier entry to the later entry; PU-01 contradicts
+the two coordinate equalities.  Thus every admissible list has length at most
+`n²` whenever `2 ≤ n`.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-03:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-04:BEGIN -->
+### PU-04 — the zero and one edge cases
+
+When `n = 0`, any list member would have coordinate zero in `Icc 1 0`, which
+is impossible.  When `n = 1`, every coordinate equals one; two list members
+would violate PU-01 through pairwise increase.  The two branches give the
+same bound `s.length ≤ n²` without any asymptotic assumption.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-04:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-05:BEGIN -->
+### PU-05 — bounded supremum closure
+
+The three parameter cases combine into `admissible_length_le_sq`.  The empty
+list is admissible, so the defining set of natural lengths is nonempty, and
+`admissible_lengths_bdd` supplies the common upper bound.  Unfolding
+`maximalLength` and applying `csSup_le` proves
+`maximalLength n ≤ n²` for every `n`.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-05:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-06:BEGIN -->
+### PU-06 — signed Big-O witness and denominator relaxation
+
+Let `f n = (Real.iteratedLog n : ℝ)` and `Ω n = -|f n|`.  Norm invariance
+under absolute value and negation gives `f =O[atTop] Ω` directly from
+`isBigO_refl`.  Since `-|f n| ≤ 0`, `0 < exp (-|f n|) ≤ 1`.  Multiplying by
+the nonnegative square and using `le_div_iff₀` turns the quadratic bound into
+`F n ≤ n² / exp (Ω n)`.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-06:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-07:BEGIN -->
+### PU-07 — exact machine root
+
+`theorem_complete` introduces the signed witness, proves its Big-O component,
+and proves the pointwise component using PU-05 and PU-06.  `Audit.lean`
+elaborates the root and both identity transports at trust level zero.  The
+result is a proof of the literal frozen proposition; a future migration that
+adds `0 ≤ Ω` would be a different statement and is intentionally not silently
+claimed here.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-07:END -->
+
+## Trust and provenance boundary
+
+The provider source is statement/definition authority only.  The local Lean
+root imports Mathlib and the replayed utility definition, never the provider
+module or its `sorryAx` declaration.  A clean `--trust=0` replay reports the
+ordinary pinned-Lean foundations `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and
+`Quot.sound`; no claim-specific axiom, unsafe declaration, opaque oracle, or
+bodyless proof is present.  The worker recommendation remains provisional
+until the canonical Master independently validates the harvested bytes.
