+# Build validation — S5-CLM-00003493
+
+The worker receipt records the executable validation basis.  Commands were
+run offline from the task-local worktree; Lean outputs were directed to a
+fresh temporary root and compiled with `--trust=0`.
+
+```text
+/usr/bin/python3 -I -B -c pass
+elan run lean --trust=0 -R <fresh-root> Statement.lean
+elan run lean --trust=0 -R <fresh-root> Proof.lean
+elan run lean --trust=0 -R <fresh-root> Audit.lean
+forbidden-token scan over the three target Lean files
+strict JSON, seal, graph, and anchor-digest audit
+mutation suite (authority, statement, anchor, graph, and axiom cases)
+```
+
+The prescribed claim self-check and all cold compilation/audit commands exit
+zero.  The audit output includes the three exact-type checks and the ordinary
+foundation census shown in `machine-checked-audit.md`; no `sorryAx` is observed
+in the target closure.  Exact command argv digests, output digests, source
+read-trace, artifact hashes, and mutation outcomes are recorded in
+`receipts/current-validation.json`.
+
+This is intentionally a worker-level, provisional validation.  The canonical
+Master must replay the harvested bytes in the integrated repository and compare
+all content-addressed bindings before any underscore-to-x promotion.
